/P 124 0 R
/E (Dengue fever is a major public health concern in Sri Lanka, and predicting the number of dengue cases can support early preventive actions and effective planning. For our study,dengue case data were taken from the National Dengue Control Unit, while location information \(latitude, longitude, elevation\) came from a Kaggle dataset, and weather data were collected using the Open Meteo Historical Weather API.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Our analysis includes descriptive statistics, graphs, tables, hypothesis testing, and multiple regression models. These methods allow us to explore patterns in the data and identify important factors that may influence dengue cases. The results will provide useful insights for understanding the relationship between environmental conditions and dengue incidence in Sri Lanka. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [15 16]
>>
endobj
