/P 125 0 R
/E (The core issue this study seeks to address is the lack of integrated approaches that combine health, geographical, and weather data to predict dengue incidence at the regional level. To bridge this gap, we employ both statistical analysis and predictive modeling techniques, enabling a more comprehensive understanding of the factors driving dengue transmission. Without such integrated models, health authorities struggle to anticipate outbreaks and allocate resources effectively.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
