/E (Research on dengue in Sri Lanka has employed diverse statistical methodologies to understand disease patterns and predict outbreaks. A 2022 study done by Arachchi and Peiris utilized time-series analysis through ARIMA modeling to forecast weekly dengue incidence in Colombo District from 2015 to 2020, demonstrating the efficiency of autoregressive models in epidemiological forecasting. https://rda.sliit.lk/entities/publication/b54dd389-c1c7-437c-a5be-13556a5d4f55)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0 733 0 R]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 734 0 R
/E (A 2019 investigation applied both Poisson and Negative Binomial regression models to analyze monthly dengue cases from 2010 to 2018, determining that the Negative Binomial model better accommodated overdispersion in count data, with rainfall emerging as a critical predictor including lag effects. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
