/E (The histogram of precipitation reveals a positively skewed distribution, with most observations concentrated at lower rainfall levels and fewer instances of heavy precipitation. This indicates that light to moderate rainfall conditions dominate the study period, while extreme rainfall events are relatively rare. Such skewness suggests that precipitation data may not follow a normal distribution and could influence statistical modeling if not appropriately handled. The limited frequency of very high rainfall values may also contribute to the weak direct association observed between precipitation and dengue incidence.)
