351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (Dengue fever is a major public health concern in many tropical and subtropical regions, where climatic conditions play a crucial role in influencing the transmission dynamics of the disease. Weather variables such as temperature, rainfall, and humidity affect the breeding, survival, and activity of Aedes mosquitoes, the primary vectors of dengue. Variations in these environmental factors can therefore lead to fluctuations in dengue incidence over time. Understanding the relationship between weather conditions and dengue cases is essential for developing effective early warning systems and targeted vector control strategies.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
